// Simulation filelist for the RTL that actually goes to silicon.
//
// Identical to ahb_QSPI_SIM.flist except for the cache RAM model: this one
// pulls logical/cache_models/tsmc65/cache_ram.v and the real precompiled
// TSMC65 macros instead of the behavioural generic model.
//
// Why this exists: ahb_QSPI_ASIC.flist was previously consumed only by
// syn/asic (synthesis + Formality) and never simulated, while every sim
// path -- UVM, cocotb, CDC -- used the generic model. The generic model's
// p_flash_cache_f0_sp_ram has no GWEN port and no write mask, so it cannot
// exercise those pins at all. That gap let a tag-RAM GWEN connection bug
// reach a P&R netlist undetected. Run the regression against this flist so
// the silicon-bound RTL is covered.

-f $(SOCLABS_AHB_QSPI_DIR)/flist/Top/ahb_QSPI.flist
-f $(SOCLABS_AHB_QSPI_DIR)/flist/VIP/ahb_QSPI_VIP.flist

$(SOCLABS_AHB_QSPI_DIR)/logical/cache_models/tsmc65/cache_ram.v

/research/precompiled_mems/TSMC65/flash_cache_data/flash_cache_data.v
/research/precompiled_mems/TSMC65/flash_cache_tag/flash_cache_tag.v

$(SOCLABS_AHB_QSPI_DIR)/pad_level/generic/ahb_qspi_pads.v
